WEBVTT

00:02.750 --> 00:06.500
The great Demon Lord Thor
was taken down by a lone hero.

00:06.830 --> 00:11.460
And so, in the interest of finding a new lord,
the demonkin organize an athletic competition.

00:11.460 --> 00:15.380
However, among the participants
is a human hero known as Helck.

00:15.920 --> 00:19.500
This alerts one of the Empire's Four Elite Lords,
Vermilio the Red,

00:19.500 --> 00:22.170
who becomes wary
and suspicious of the hero.

00:22.710 --> 00:26.040
Meanwhile, the other
Demon Lord known as Urum,

00:26.040 --> 00:30.210
falls in battle against a horde
of winged knights clad in white.

00:57.420 --> 00:59.670
Kurui dashita haguruma ga

00:59.670 --> 01:02.330
Kanakirigoe de sakendeiru

01:02.330 --> 01:04.380
Hibana o chirasu unmei

01:04.380 --> 01:07.210
Moeagaru suki o ukagau mitai

01:07.460 --> 01:09.540
Yabai card hikiateta

01:09.540 --> 01:12.170
Pinch no toki koso chance da

01:12.170 --> 01:14.080
Mada akiramete nanka nai

01:14.080 --> 01:16.960
Saigo made tatsu mono ga shousha da

01:17.170 --> 01:19.330
Hohoemi kakeru akuma

01:19.330 --> 01:22.080
To te o toriatte odorou

01:22.080 --> 01:24.330
Narifuri kamau koto wa nai

01:24.330 --> 01:26.670
Gekijou ni yuragu ketsui

01:26.670 --> 01:29.630
Yami ni nomarete shimau mae ni

01:29.830 --> 01:30.500
Break it

01:30.500 --> 01:32.000
Keriagero

01:32.000 --> 01:35.080
Kudakechiru no wa kimi no joushiki da

01:35.080 --> 01:39.580
Dare ni mo makenai honoo kokoro ni daite

01:39.880 --> 01:45.330
Ima hateshinai sekai ni sasageru kono inori ga

01:45.330 --> 01:50.080
Kanau asu ga kuru made taeru koto naku

01:50.080 --> 01:51.710
Moyashi tsuzukeru

01:51.710 --> 01:54.580
It's my soul

02:01.960 --> 02:06.880
<b>Anne from Management</b>

02:13.630 --> 02:15.920
Something weird is going on
with the humans,

02:15.920 --> 02:18.880
which means we need to get rid
of this Helck guy ASAP.

02:18.880 --> 02:19.710
Hon!

02:20.080 --> 02:22.920
You're absolutely sure
this race idea of yours will work?

02:23.920 --> 02:25.290
Of course, ma'am!

02:25.290 --> 02:29.420
I've prepared a rather unique steed
for Helck to race on, you see.

02:29.920 --> 02:32.670
So I'm quite confident
we'll get rid of him this time!

02:32.670 --> 02:33.670
Oh?

02:35.130 --> 02:36.250
Fair enough.

02:36.250 --> 02:39.880
It's true that the outcome of this match
will hinge mostly on the quality of the horse.

02:39.880 --> 02:42.960
Not even Helck can do much if his ride
ends up being weak.

02:43.420 --> 02:45.750
Ah, the participants are making their entrance now.

02:55.000 --> 02:55.960
Aw yeah! Let's go Helck!

02:55.960 --> 02:56.580
Now things are exciting!
Aw yeah! Let's go Helck!<b></b>

02:56.580 --> 02:57.960
Now things are exciting!

03:02.750 --> 03:03.670
What do you think?

03:03.670 --> 03:06.170
Surely he won't be getting very far
with a steed like that!

03:06.170 --> 03:08.790
You fool! Just think about
Helck's popularity for a second!

03:08.790 --> 03:11.880
There's no way that kind of blatant scheme
is gonna fly with the audience!

03:12.040 --> 03:15.580
Hot damn, Helck is massive!
He makes the horse look tiny!

03:15.580 --> 03:18.380
A big body to fit his big heart!
Helck's the best!

03:18.380 --> 03:20.960
I wanna be a macho man just like him!

03:20.960 --> 03:22.330
Are these people all right in the head?

03:23.000 --> 03:25.630
Uh, th-they're just very positive thinkers!

03:26.000 --> 03:28.040
Okay, everyone, thanks for your patience!

03:28.040 --> 03:30.170
Rococo the announcer here!

03:30.170 --> 03:34.080
I hope you like surprises because the next stage
of competition is going to be a race!

03:34.960 --> 03:37.170
How can he look so damn carefree?!

03:38.380 --> 03:41.460
Does he really think he can win
with that pathetic horse?

03:42.710 --> 03:46.250
Here's the race course and, trust me,
there'll be plenty of obstacles along the way!

03:46.250 --> 03:47.880
After completing the loop and heading back,

03:47.880 --> 03:50.330
the first four racers to arrive here
will move on to the finals!

03:50.330 --> 03:52.040
Should be exciting!

03:52.040 --> 03:54.170
That didn't even take a minute to explain!

03:54.170 --> 03:55.750
Sweet! Now get this thing started!

03:56.130 --> 03:58.790
Competitors, are you ready?

04:03.000 --> 04:05.880
3... 2... 1...

04:10.420 --> 04:13.290
And there you have it,
all the horses have now crossed the start-

04:13.290 --> 04:14.380
Or not.

04:23.540 --> 04:25.880
I guess all that confidence was just for show!

04:25.880 --> 04:28.710
There's nothing that Helck can do
to get himself out of this mess now!

04:29.080 --> 04:31.330
Helck is stuck at a standstill!

04:31.330 --> 04:33.750
He seemed like a shoo-in,
but now things are looking very bleak for him!

04:33.920 --> 04:37.080
There was a lottery to decide
which horses we got assigned.

04:37.080 --> 04:40.250
Too bad, Helck!
Seems like luck wasn't on your side this time!

04:40.250 --> 04:43.330
Management obviously
screwed him over on purpose.

04:43.330 --> 04:45.670
But since he's one of those
infernal human heroes,

04:45.670 --> 04:47.080
he definitely had it coming.

04:47.250 --> 04:50.880
Well shucks! Helck is left with no choice
but to get off his steed!

04:51.830 --> 04:54.670
Why doesn't he just give up here and now?

04:55.130 --> 04:57.960
He can't seriously expect
to turn things around, can he?

04:59.920 --> 05:02.920
Seems like the frontrunners
have just entered the obstacle course.

05:02.920 --> 05:06.210
So I'll be focusing
my commentary over there now.

05:06.750 --> 05:09.290
There is zero chance
of Helck winning at this point.

05:09.290 --> 05:12.330
Why don't we go see how
the frontrunners are fairing, ma'am?

05:19.420 --> 05:20.210
Poor thing.

05:20.210 --> 05:22.710
That cannon fire at the start
really freaked you out, huh?

05:22.710 --> 05:24.080
Well, it's no problem.

05:24.380 --> 05:26.420
Listen, everything's okay now.

05:26.420 --> 05:28.330
We're gonna turn this situation around.

05:28.580 --> 05:31.830
Don't worry a hair on your little head.
We'll definitely catch up with everyone else!

05:31.830 --> 05:33.790
Your body may be quite small,

05:33.790 --> 05:36.420
but it's actually hiding
an immense power deep inside.

05:37.380 --> 05:40.080
Just trust me. I can tell.

05:40.380 --> 05:42.170
You have what it takes.

05:42.170 --> 05:43.880
You can do this.

05:44.210 --> 05:45.500
Without a doubt!

05:52.580 --> 05:54.710
Man, these are some sick traps they cooked up!

05:54.710 --> 05:55.790
How dull.

05:56.420 --> 05:59.250
The obstacle course is filled with stuff
that'll send you home with serious injuries!

05:59.250 --> 06:00.960
And it's giving our competitors a really hard time!

06:01.130 --> 06:04.960
Luckily, we have a medical team at the ready!
So please keep charging full steam ahead!

06:04.960 --> 06:06.880
This obstacle course is pretty hardcore.

06:06.880 --> 06:08.830
It may be rough on the other participants,

06:08.830 --> 06:10.920
but it was designed as part
of our anti-Helck measures.

06:16.750 --> 06:17.710
Watch it!

06:17.710 --> 06:19.170
What the hell is your problem, jackass?!

06:19.170 --> 06:21.130
There's no need for me to be number one,

06:21.130 --> 06:23.830
but having someone run in front of me
really gets on my nerves.

06:23.830 --> 06:26.040
Do yourself a favor and fall behind me already.

06:26.040 --> 06:26.880
Like hell I will!

06:27.170 --> 06:29.290
That's Hyura and Kenros.

06:29.290 --> 06:31.830
They've both made it through this competition
with a spectacular track record.

06:31.830 --> 06:35.330
Especially Hyura, her combat level is top-class.

06:35.330 --> 06:38.670
The new Demon Lord is almost assuredly
going to be one of them.

06:39.170 --> 06:41.290
Well, let's hope it stays that way...

06:41.290 --> 06:42.130
Huh?

06:46.630 --> 06:48.000
Big news, folks!

06:48.000 --> 06:50.250
Helck was stuck at the start line earlier,

06:50.250 --> 06:52.710
but now he's zooming across the track
on his way to a major comeback!

06:52.710 --> 06:54.210
I FRIGGIN' KNEW IT!

06:54.210 --> 06:57.420
There was no way he'd just surrender
without putting up a fight!

06:57.540 --> 07:00.540
But how could that tiny horse
move at such high speeds?

07:00.540 --> 07:02.290
I don't believe it!

07:10.080 --> 07:11.250
Hold on a damn minute!

07:11.250 --> 07:13.290
Look! He's just running along with it!

07:13.290 --> 07:14.500
Oh, you're right.

07:14.500 --> 07:17.960
He's taking advantage of the fact
his feet can reach the ground. How clever!

07:17.960 --> 07:20.130
That's not clever! IT'S CHEATING!

07:20.130 --> 07:21.540
This is a HORSE race, dammit!

07:21.670 --> 07:23.960
He's breaking the rules!
Disqualify him right now!

07:23.960 --> 07:26.750
But falling from your horse isn't grounds
for disqualification in the rules.

07:26.750 --> 07:30.130
We might upset everyone
if we try to eject him for that reason alone...

07:30.130 --> 07:32.920
Aw jeez, you only worry about the pettiest crap!

07:32.920 --> 07:34.750
But please, rest assured!

07:34.750 --> 07:37.920
We still have the obstacle course
that's been making all the other participants suffer!

07:37.920 --> 07:40.920
And he'll surely have a hard time avoiding
the traps with that horse dragging him down!

07:42.630 --> 07:43.710
He destroyed it!

07:43.710 --> 07:46.130
DO YOU KNOW HOW HARD
THOSE ARE TO MAKE?!

07:50.420 --> 07:52.420
At this rate, he'll end up
leading the pack in no time!

07:52.420 --> 07:54.540
O-oh dear, this isn't good...

07:54.540 --> 07:56.290
There has to be something we can do!

07:57.380 --> 08:00.920
The frontrunners are currently
making their way through the old mining area.

08:01.170 --> 08:02.380
Uh-oh! Rebero's in trouble!

08:02.380 --> 08:04.790
He just fell off the unsteady suspension bridge!

08:04.790 --> 08:05.710
That's it!

08:05.710 --> 08:07.080
Hon! The suspension bridge!

08:07.080 --> 08:08.790
We have to find a way to make Helck fall off it!

08:08.790 --> 08:11.170
Is there anything nearby that we could use?!

08:11.170 --> 08:14.380
Um, well, there's a stockpile of explosives
that were used for mining...

08:14.380 --> 08:15.130
Perfect!

08:15.130 --> 08:18.130
Then rig all of it to explode
right in the middle of the bridge!

08:18.920 --> 08:22.540
Then cover the nearby path in oil
to keep them from staying on their feet!

08:22.790 --> 08:24.960
Falling off the bridge
will cost him a huge chunk of time!

08:24.960 --> 08:26.630
Then he'll lose for sure!

08:26.630 --> 08:28.500
I'll make the preparations right away.

08:28.750 --> 08:31.080
Lord Hon just issued us emergency orders!

08:31.080 --> 08:33.210
Let's hurry and get this trap set up!

08:33.210 --> 08:36.170
The management staff have gotten to work on it.

08:36.460 --> 08:38.290
Now this is what I call a slip and slide!

08:38.290 --> 08:40.920
Once we're done here,
all that's left is rigging the bombs to explode!

08:40.920 --> 08:42.540
As easy as pie!

08:44.790 --> 08:46.290
Whoa! What're you doing?!

08:46.290 --> 08:48.130
Stay back!

08:51.380 --> 08:52.750
NO!

08:52.750 --> 08:54.250
WHAT ARE THOSE IDIOTS DOING?!

08:54.250 --> 08:57.630
The plan won't work unless the bridge
explodes right as Helck is trying to cross it!

08:57.630 --> 08:59.750
There's no fixing this, you fool!

08:59.750 --> 09:03.540
B-but you know, Helck will be stuck
if there is no bridge for him to cross...

09:03.540 --> 09:04.750
So it all works out in the end!

09:05.040 --> 09:06.040
Wrong!

09:06.040 --> 09:07.960
Giving him the chance to act
is a huge mistake!

09:07.960 --> 09:10.420
Because he'll just find a way
to keep moving, bridge or not!

09:11.210 --> 09:12.380
See! He jumped!

09:14.040 --> 09:15.710
Here comes Helck!
He's making this look easy!

09:15.710 --> 09:17.960
And now he's running
without even riding his horse!

09:17.960 --> 09:19.080
What a trailblazer!

09:19.080 --> 09:21.040
At least straddle it, dammit!

09:21.250 --> 09:23.380
He's zipping past the competition
one after the other!

09:23.380 --> 09:25.580
And now he's knocking on the frontrunner's door!

09:36.210 --> 09:37.630
I knew you'd show up, Helck!

09:37.630 --> 09:40.290
Seriously?
How did he manage to close the gap?

09:40.290 --> 09:42.130
Is he a fast runner on top of everything else?!

09:53.290 --> 09:54.540
Catch ya later!

09:56.540 --> 09:57.630
Look at him go!

09:57.630 --> 10:00.830
And with that,
Helck has finally taken the top spot!

10:00.830 --> 10:02.170
What a badass!

10:02.170 --> 10:04.790
That guy totally breaks the mold
in every sense of the word!

10:04.790 --> 10:06.290
This is so hype!

10:06.830 --> 10:07.790
I'ma copy him.

10:08.330 --> 10:11.500
I guarantee you that I've got the fastest legs
in the entire empire!

10:11.500 --> 10:13.500
So I'm not shying away
from a challenge like this!

10:13.710 --> 10:16.790
Holy smokes, look at Kenros!
He just jumped down from his steed!

10:18.290 --> 10:19.920
What could he possibly be thinking?!

10:19.920 --> 10:22.210
And now he's making a mad dash
for the finish line!

10:22.210 --> 10:23.830
I'm fine with third place.

10:24.750 --> 10:27.210
This is nuts!
Kenros is quickly closing the gap!

10:27.210 --> 10:29.830
He's running even faster than Helck!

10:36.880 --> 10:38.670
And Helck takes it!

10:39.170 --> 10:42.000
Helck speeds across
the finish line like an arrow!

10:42.790 --> 10:45.580
Kenros was right on his tail,
but it wasn't enough!

10:45.580 --> 10:48.630
Still, what an amazing show of talent
up until the very end!

10:48.630 --> 10:49.670
Damn!

10:49.670 --> 10:52.580
Never imagined that you'd beat me in a race, too.

10:52.580 --> 10:54.000
Don't be ridiculous!

10:54.000 --> 10:57.500
We both know that I'd have lost
if you had gone all out from the start.

10:57.500 --> 11:00.830
You are such a cool dude!
C'mon, let's go out for drinks!

11:00.830 --> 11:02.540
We're gonna celebrate getting into the finals!

11:03.790 --> 11:05.580
Ya gotta hand it to Helck!

11:05.580 --> 11:07.170
Helck's the man! Oh yeah!

11:07.170 --> 11:09.290
You were awesome, too, Kenros!

11:09.290 --> 11:12.250
Gosh, his ability to surmount
any obstacle is just mind-boggling.

11:15.000 --> 11:17.670
Friggin' hell...

11:17.670 --> 11:20.630
I have a barrier set and ready!
She's free to blow her top whenever!

11:20.630 --> 11:23.170
Lady Vermilio, do you have a moment?

11:25.790 --> 11:27.630
Sure, Ista. What is it?

11:27.630 --> 11:29.290
Huh? Is she done?

11:29.290 --> 11:33.040
The scheduled report from our reconnaissance squadron
at Castle Urum has just come in.

11:33.040 --> 11:35.960
All right, here is fine. Go ahead.

11:35.960 --> 11:38.580
Huh, I feel kinda lonely now...

11:38.710 --> 11:41.130
The castle remains quiet and undisturbed.

11:41.130 --> 11:43.880
There is no sign of the enemy
preparing to make a march on us.

11:43.880 --> 11:44.920
Hmm.

11:47.250 --> 11:50.290
Furthermore, they managed
to infiltrate the castle grounds without issue.

11:50.790 --> 11:54.960
Per the report, not a single human
has been sighted anywhere that they've looked.

11:55.380 --> 11:58.750
But they did confirm the presence of
103 winged knights stationed throughout the castle.

11:58.750 --> 12:03.000
And among those, they've spotted one
who appears to be acting as leader.

12:03.290 --> 12:04.250
Hmm.

12:04.920 --> 12:07.290
Their forces are smaller in number
than we anticipated.

12:07.630 --> 12:08.630
Yes.

12:08.630 --> 12:12.460
No doubt thanks to Lord Urum thinning out their ranks
as he fought until the bitter end.

12:13.920 --> 12:16.540
But it really doesn't matter
how many knights they've lost,

12:16.540 --> 12:19.750
even if they initially attacked the castle
with something like 300.

12:19.750 --> 12:21.880
We cannot let our guard down for a second.

12:21.880 --> 12:24.330
I'm still having trouble processing it.

12:24.330 --> 12:27.460
How could anyone overcome a powerful
Demon Lord with such meager numbers?

12:27.460 --> 12:29.750
Just who are these winged creatures?

12:30.380 --> 12:31.750
That remains unclear.

12:31.750 --> 12:34.710
However, we know for certain that
they came from the human realm.

12:34.710 --> 12:37.000
And also, that they're hostile.

12:37.000 --> 12:40.670
In any event, we can't just leave them
to their own devices.

12:41.040 --> 12:45.380
Honestly, part of me wants to rush over
and wipe all of those winged knights out right now.

12:45.380 --> 12:46.920
But there's still Helck to deal with.

12:46.920 --> 12:48.880
We need to plan our moves very carefully.

12:49.630 --> 12:51.830
It seems like you're in a rather tough spot.

12:54.420 --> 12:55.750
I know that voice.

12:55.750 --> 12:57.130
Is that you, Azudra?

12:57.880 --> 12:59.080
Indeed.

12:59.080 --> 13:00.080
Strange.

13:00.080 --> 13:03.830
The reason I'm here filling in for you is because
they said you were badly injured and unconscious.

13:04.210 --> 13:06.040
But you sound pretty dandy to me.

13:06.880 --> 13:08.750
You know how people like to exaggerate.

13:08.750 --> 13:11.580
I'm sorry for heaping so much trouble
on your plate, Vermikins.

13:11.580 --> 13:13.920
I thought I told you to stop calling me that.

13:15.040 --> 13:16.500
Ah yes, that you did.

13:16.500 --> 13:19.670
But it was so long ago now
that it slipped my mind.

13:19.670 --> 13:21.630
Just state your business and be done with it.

13:22.210 --> 13:26.000
It's about those winged knights,
and our hero friend Helck...

13:26.000 --> 13:29.130
I have an idea that I hope
you're willing to listen to.

13:29.960 --> 13:31.080
Oh?

13:31.080 --> 13:34.080
<b>Combat Level: 73</b>

13:31.080 --> 13:34.080
<b>Four Elite Lords of the Empire:</b>

13:31.090 --> 13:34.080
<b>Azudra the Blue</b>

13:34.380 --> 13:36.540
The final match will be to-

13:37.580 --> 13:39.130
GET SOME REST!

13:40.290 --> 13:41.130
Dammit, man!

13:41.130 --> 13:42.830
Why did you drag yourself all the way here?!

13:42.830 --> 13:44.210
You need to stay in bed and recover!

13:44.210 --> 13:45.880
I've called the paramedic team...

13:46.380 --> 13:48.580
Jeez, you never change.

13:48.880 --> 13:52.000
Come on, just hear me out
for a second, Vermikins.

13:52.000 --> 13:54.460
Quit calling me that already!
Or I'll burn you to ash!

13:54.670 --> 13:58.420
The final match of the competition...
will be to retake Castle Urum.

13:58.750 --> 14:00.330
Whoever can defeat the enemy leader

14:00.330 --> 14:03.630
and reclaim the castle for us
shall be crowned the new Demon Lord.

14:05.500 --> 14:07.670
It's two birds with one stone.

14:07.920 --> 14:10.880
We can quickly subdue
the army of winged knights.

14:11.080 --> 14:12.380
And at the same time...

14:12.920 --> 14:16.290
we can test whether Helck is truly willing
to fight on our side or not.

14:16.290 --> 14:18.080
This'll bring his real motivations to light.

14:18.580 --> 14:19.540
Ridiculous!

14:19.540 --> 14:21.040
We're talking about a human here!

14:21.040 --> 14:23.710
You're just putting the other participants
in needless danger!

14:23.710 --> 14:26.080
Helck may be a hero from the human realm,

14:26.080 --> 14:28.710
but a deep-seated hatred for humans
has led him to try and eradicate them.

14:28.710 --> 14:30.540
It's perfectly possible that whole story is true.

14:30.540 --> 14:32.710
Talk is cheap because it's easy to do!

14:32.710 --> 14:34.500
I wouldn't trust him for a minute!

14:34.500 --> 14:37.420
Indeed. Words alone
are not enough to garner trust.

14:37.420 --> 14:42.250
Which is exactly why I came up with the idea
of having him fight against those winged knights.

14:43.000 --> 14:46.130
Those knights are clearly hostile to us.

14:46.670 --> 14:51.130
So if Helck actually steps up to defeat them,
and even retake Castle Urum for us,

14:51.500 --> 14:54.750
then it might just be worth
putting some faith in him.

14:55.580 --> 14:56.710
Interesting.

14:56.710 --> 14:58.960
So that's why you proposed this idea.

14:58.960 --> 15:02.750
But we still don't know whether those winged knights
are part of the humans' forces or not.

15:02.750 --> 15:04.580
I don't see how it's worth putting any faith in him!

15:06.290 --> 15:08.080
Helck is a threat.

15:08.080 --> 15:10.000
If we're forced to go up against him in battle,

15:10.000 --> 15:12.000
then not even the likes of us
will come out of it unscathed.

15:12.000 --> 15:13.830
And to avoid as much harm as possible,

15:13.830 --> 15:17.540
I believe we must ascertain whether or not
he's someone that we need to eliminate.

15:19.540 --> 15:21.000
There's still time.

15:21.000 --> 15:24.460
Ponder all the options
and then let me know what you think.

15:24.460 --> 15:26.790
I'm feeling sleepy...

15:26.790 --> 15:27.920
lost too much blood...

15:27.920 --> 15:28.670
Oh dear, Lord Azudra!
lost too much blood...<b></b>

15:28.670 --> 15:29.460
Oh dear, Lord Azudra!

15:29.830 --> 15:30.880
Fool.

15:30.880 --> 15:33.630
The threat that Helck poses
is what makes him so difficult to trust!

15:35.540 --> 15:38.790
However... that's not a bad idea for the finals.

15:39.170 --> 15:42.330
We would actually be in a very advantageous
position if everything went in our favor.

15:42.330 --> 15:46.130
Not to mention, it would get Helck
away from this stadium.

15:46.460 --> 15:48.080
The only problem is...

15:49.080 --> 15:50.080
Hey!

15:50.330 --> 15:51.540
Don't fall asleep yet!

15:52.040 --> 15:53.330
Huh? Have you decided already?

15:53.330 --> 15:54.630
No! I have a question!

15:54.630 --> 15:56.790
Ah, Lord Azudra is going to die!

15:56.790 --> 15:59.420
What's the plan if Helck ends up
being our enemy?

16:02.000 --> 16:03.460
Just try and picture it.

16:03.460 --> 16:05.630
Those winged knights
will be the least of our worries

16:05.630 --> 16:07.790
if Helck turns against us
in the middle of the battle!

16:09.580 --> 16:11.790
Have no fear, I've got that covered.

16:11.790 --> 16:14.170
I did some crafting while I was in the hospital.

16:14.170 --> 16:16.670
Ta-da! This is the Deep-Green Ring!

16:16.670 --> 16:20.710
Making all the competitors wear this will prevent them
from bringing any harm to one another!

16:21.170 --> 16:23.420
You really have thought this through, huh?

16:23.420 --> 16:27.130
Amazing as always, Lord Azudra!
Nothing is too much for you!

16:27.130 --> 16:28.420
You can say that again.

16:28.420 --> 16:31.290
But I really wish he'd use all that power of his
to do something about Helck.

16:31.290 --> 16:33.500
Oh please, that's just impossible.

16:33.500 --> 16:35.040
If I were to do anything,

16:35.040 --> 16:38.330
the absolute best that I could do
is buy us some time just like I'm doing now.

16:40.290 --> 16:43.830
At any rate, this should cover all our bases
in regards to Helck!

16:43.830 --> 16:44.920
Mm-hmm.

16:44.920 --> 16:46.130
That may be so,

16:46.130 --> 16:49.330
but it doesn't change the fact that we
have to confront all of those winged knights.

16:49.670 --> 16:51.130
It's still very worrisome.

16:51.420 --> 16:52.420
True.

16:52.420 --> 16:54.540
Something unpredictable is bound to happen.

16:54.540 --> 16:57.380
So I propose that we send someone formidable
along with them who can handle

16:57.380 --> 16:59.380
any potentially disastrous situations.

16:59.380 --> 17:01.250
Someone formidable?

17:01.630 --> 17:02.670
Yes.

17:03.830 --> 17:05.250
Uh, so...

17:05.630 --> 17:06.670
Vermikins?

17:06.670 --> 17:08.290
CUT THAT OUT ALREADY!

17:08.830 --> 17:10.040
Very well, then.

17:10.960 --> 17:12.130
I get it.

17:12.960 --> 17:15.580
Helck is also the threat
I'm most concerned about.

17:15.580 --> 17:17.750
So you didn't even need to bring this up.

17:17.750 --> 17:21.000
I was already thinking about staying close by
to quickly intervene if things go south.

17:22.040 --> 17:23.750
If Helck proves to be an enemy,

17:24.250 --> 17:26.920
then I will put my life on the line
to terminate him!

17:30.000 --> 17:34.380
I can't help but feel it's wrong of me to laze around
while you're out there flirting with danger!

17:34.380 --> 17:36.250
Perhaps if I summon up
enough willpower I could also...

17:36.250 --> 17:37.170
Stay in bed.

17:38.290 --> 17:40.250
Don't worry about the participants either.

17:40.250 --> 17:42.750
I'll take on the responsibility of keeping them safe.

17:43.040 --> 17:46.460
You just stay focused on recuperating,
and get back in action as soon as possible.

17:46.460 --> 17:49.040
Gosh, I really have such great friends!

17:49.040 --> 17:51.830
I truly appreciate this, Vermikins!

17:52.710 --> 17:57.290
HOW MANY GODDAMN TIMES DO I HAVE
TO TELL YOU NOT TO CALL ME THAT?!

17:57.880 --> 18:00.250
<b>5 Days Later</b>

18:02.080 --> 18:03.580
Okay, everybody!

18:04.170 --> 18:07.380
I see that you've all put
your Deep-Green Rings on.

18:08.000 --> 18:11.330
<b>Combat Level: 45</b>

18:08.000 --> 18:11.330
<b>Dorshe the Indestructible</b>

18:08.130 --> 18:09.420
So without further ado,

18:09.920 --> 18:12.960
it's time to announce the details
of the championship match!

18:12.960 --> 18:14.460
For the finals you will be...

18:14.790 --> 18:17.290
retaking Castle Urum!

18:19.210 --> 18:20.290
Wow.

18:20.580 --> 18:21.790
Just the four of us?

18:21.790 --> 18:23.250
That's right!

18:23.250 --> 18:26.080
This is stupid.
Why can't I just be out there from the start?

18:27.000 --> 18:28.750
For the dramatic flare, of course!

18:28.750 --> 18:31.580
It's much more exciting to have you
make a grand appearance later, you know?

18:31.580 --> 18:33.420
I don't think excitement is necessary here...

18:34.250 --> 18:37.290
Anyway, just take a look
at how confident they all are!

18:37.710 --> 18:39.920
Finally, a regular fight.

18:39.920 --> 18:41.540
I'm actually happy to hear it.

18:41.960 --> 18:45.420
I guess this is going to be a battle
to avenge the fallen Lord Urum.

18:45.630 --> 18:50.290
They don't even have the slightest reservation about
facing the forces who took down a Demon Lord!

18:50.290 --> 18:52.830
Uh, actually, one of them
looks pretty stressed out...

18:53.130 --> 18:54.750
Man, I am so dead.

18:56.330 --> 18:59.170
Hard to tell what's going through
Helck's head, huh?

18:59.170 --> 19:00.460
What kind of look is that?

19:00.460 --> 19:02.960
Are we sure he isn't just
sleeping with his eyes open?!

19:02.960 --> 19:04.920
But please have no fear!

19:04.920 --> 19:08.750
Those of us on the management staff know it's
our responsibility to keep all the participants safe!

19:08.750 --> 19:12.040
Which is why a very powerful warrior
will be accompanying us there!

19:12.040 --> 19:15.000
Whew! You should have started with that!
Now I feel better!

19:15.000 --> 19:16.080
Alrighty then!

19:16.080 --> 19:18.380
Let's get straight to the introduction!

19:18.380 --> 19:21.500
The person who will be keeping us all safe is...
Miss Anne!

19:28.420 --> 19:31.330
I'm Anne from management. Nice to meet you.

19:29.210 --> 19:31.290
<b>Acting Level: 2</b>

19:29.210 --> 19:31.290
<b>Anne from Management (Alias)</b>

19:31.330 --> 19:34.750
And here I thought she would try
acting more like a commoner...

19:34.750 --> 19:37.210
Welp, that's Lady Vermilio for you.
Steady as a rock.

19:37.210 --> 19:40.630
The enemies that you'll be fighting were
formidable enough to defeat Demon Lord Urum.

19:40.630 --> 19:42.710
It won't be an easy battle by any means,

19:42.710 --> 19:45.710
but I'm certain that you're all strong enough
to come out the victors.

19:45.710 --> 19:48.080
The title of Demon Lord is up for grabs,
so give it your all.

19:48.080 --> 19:49.960
Clap, clap, clap.

19:52.630 --> 19:54.170
Thanks for the applause.

19:54.830 --> 19:56.170
What? There's only one?

19:56.170 --> 19:57.170
That's right!

19:57.170 --> 20:00.290
But she's super-duper strong,
so you have nothing to worry about!

20:00.500 --> 20:03.250
You know, she seems oddly familiar...

20:03.250 --> 20:05.580
Well, they say never
judge a book by its cover!

20:09.040 --> 20:10.420
You there...

20:11.580 --> 20:12.880
What is it?

20:12.880 --> 20:15.330
You're the judge from the cooking contest!

20:15.330 --> 20:17.540
Oh. That explains it.

20:17.540 --> 20:18.580
She couldn't be!

20:18.580 --> 20:20.460
I mean, her hair is way shorter!

20:20.460 --> 20:23.040
No, that was me. I just cut my hair.

20:24.580 --> 20:25.750
Actually, wait.

20:25.750 --> 20:29.080
She seemed oddly familiar
when I saw her on the judges panel, too...

20:29.080 --> 20:30.380
I wish I could remember.

20:31.000 --> 20:33.330
I'm Helck! It's a pleasure!

20:37.130 --> 20:39.670
She looks incredibly appalled by him...

20:39.670 --> 20:40.540
Is she just being wary?

20:40.750 --> 20:42.630
I'm Helck! It's a pleasure!

20:42.630 --> 20:45.000
Jeez, he's as stubborn as a mule.

20:56.500 --> 20:58.290
Yeah, same here...

21:19.710 --> 21:22.500
Yakusoku suru yo

21:22.500 --> 21:25.460
Itsuka sekai ga

21:25.460 --> 21:27.540
Owaru toki mata

21:27.540 --> 21:30.170
Deaemasu you ni

21:42.250 --> 21:47.630
Hana no you na hito datta to

21:47.630 --> 21:53.540
Dareka ga chiisaku tsubuyaiteita

21:53.540 --> 21:59.080
Mizu no nai heya soredemo tashika ni

21:59.080 --> 22:01.580
Asu e saiteita

22:03.290 --> 22:06.080
Zenbu yume dattara

22:06.080 --> 22:08.960
Kimi o shiru koto mo

22:08.960 --> 22:11.880
Koi o suru koto mo

22:11.880 --> 22:15.380
Ikiru imi sae shirazu ni

22:16.210 --> 22:19.000
Tatoeba asu ga

22:19.000 --> 22:21.710
Donna ame demo

22:21.710 --> 22:24.080
Yoru wa ake sekai ni

22:24.080 --> 22:27.170
Niji ga kakaru you ni

22:27.540 --> 22:30.250
Mune no itami mo

22:30.250 --> 22:33.130
Tsutau namida mo

22:33.130 --> 22:36.580
Mirai e no tane ni kaete

22:36.580 --> 22:38.210
Ikiyou

22:38.920 --> 22:40.960
Bukiyou na ai ga

22:40.960 --> 22:44.130
Hana o sakasu made

22:45.920 --> 22:50.710
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:45.920 --> 22:50.710
<b>The Unknown Enemy</b>

22:46.670 --> 22:49.420
Next time: "The Unknown Enemy"
